[preflight] console: fix the environment problem named above, then rerun
    fugaro setup
[project/gcp] command: Billing is not linked to acme-prod yet, so setup paused here: the project and Firebase exist, and what needs billing (Cloud Run, Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, the buckets) waits for it. If you cannot link it yourself, forward this to whoever administers billing in your organization: they run the first line below with their billing account's id (theirs to supply; they find it with gcloud billing accounts list; see docs/gcp-setup.md#not-an-owner). Then run the second line at your own terminal: it resumes acme-prod and finishes the setup, and marks the project managed once you type its ID
    gcloud billing projects link acme-prod --billing-account=<billing-account-id>
    fugaro setup --name aurora --gcp-project acme-prod
[project/create] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, type the ID(s) it asks for after running
    fugaro setup --gcp-project acme-prod --parent folders/123 --link-billing 0123AB-4567CD-89EF01
[project/guided] command: Billing is not linked to acme-prod yet, so setup paused here: the project and Firebase exist, and what needs billing (Cloud Run, Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, the buckets) waits for it. If you cannot link it yourself, forward this to whoever administers billing in your organization: they run the first line below with their billing account's id (theirs to supply; they find it with gcloud billing accounts list; see docs/gcp-setup.md#not-an-owner). Then run the second line at your own terminal: it resumes acme-prod and finishes the setup, and marks the project managed once you type its ID
    gcloud billing projects link acme-prod --billing-account=<billing-account-id>
    fugaro setup --name aurora --gcp-project acme-prod
[installation] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, type the project's name to apply after running
    fugaro setup
[firebase] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, type the project's name at each apply after running
    fugaro setup --firebase-project <gcp-project-id>
[images] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, type the project's name to pin this release's base images and copy the release images after running
    fugaro setup
[installation-2] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, type the project's name to apply the history job after running
    fugaro setup --firebase-project <gcp-project-id>
[secrets/no-checkout] command: in a checkout of the repository, in your own terminal window, run
    fugaro setup
[secrets/github] command: run these in your own terminal window, one line at a time, in this order
    fugaro secrets set github-app-key < PATH-TO-THE-KEY-FILE
    claude setup-token
    fugaro secrets set claude-oauth-token --repo acme/app
[secrets/bitbucket] command: run these in your own terminal window, one line at a time, in this order
    fugaro secrets set bitbucket-token --repo acme/app
[secrets/odd-repo] command: run these in your own terminal window, one line at a time, in this order
    claude setup-token
    fugaro secrets set claude-oauth-token --repo 'ac me/ap'\''p'
[plugin/update] command: fugaro update-skills
[plugin/fork] command: fugaro update-skills --allow-fork
[repository] prompt: in your own terminal window, not through a coding agent or a pipe, in the checkout, type the project's name at each apply after running
    fugaro setup
[repository/onboard] command: fugaro setup --onboard-repo acme/app
[repository/onboard-odd] command: fugaro setup --onboard-repo 'acme/app;rm -rf'
[repository/unusual-host] console: in your own terminal window, or in a fresh clone of the real remote, type git.example.com/acme/app at the prompt of
    fugaro setup
[repository/switch] command: git switch -- main
[repository/switch-dash] command: git switch -- '-fix;rm -rf'
[repository/switch-quote] command: git switch -- 'it'\''s'
